Design decision: one gate method rather than a flag check at each site.
Three surfaces (steps, outputs, interrupt metadata) have to switch
together; checking the flag independently at each would let a later
change add a fourth site that ignores the opt-out. Making the helpers
take NodeProvenance rather than *session.Event enforces it structurally.

Two tests guard against over-suppression, which is the likelier bug than
under-suppression: a disabled workflow node still streams its text, and
author-driven sub-agent steps still work.

